DESCRIPTION:Organizer: Chicago Public Library\\nCost: free\\nAges: 0-60 mo
 nths\\nCategory: Film & Events\\n\\nJoin us for a screening of The Ground 
 Between Us. Following 2017 policy shifts that reduced national monuments (
 such as Bears Ears National Monument)\, rolled back environmental protecti
 ons\, and opened areas like the Arctic National Wildlife Refuge to oil and
  gas development\, the documentary looks at how everyday Americans and Nat
 ive tribal organizations in places like Alaska\, Oregon\, and Utah respond
 . © Passion River Films. - 62 minutes - Not Rated Community Cinema is at 
 a branch near you! Check\\n\\nMore info: https://chipublib.bibliocommons.c
 om/events/6aeca79aebad2200454a8ecc
